n polling or a Democratic outside-spending surge in the final weeks could push this into tossup territory.", "confidence": "low", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "The open TX-23 seat came open when Tony Gonzales resigned in April, and Republicans nominated gun-content creator Brandon Herrera over a field. The district leans Republican by about seven points, and the 2026 environment favors the GOP, giving Republicans a structural edge in a seat they have held for years.\n\nStill, the race is not straightforward. Herrera has faced damaging coverage of past remarks and delayed financial disclosures, and outside groups have spent heavily against him. Katy Padilla Stout has modest resources, and several forecasters rate the race a tossup while most call it Likely Republican. With no recent independent polling, uncertainty is high, and the race sits as a modest Republican favorite.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2428, "margin": -4.13}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2506, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.355, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.3283, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.203, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2999, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.3496, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2679, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.3125, "margin": -3.5}]}